WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.138
Lab 2 runs one mapping on
your own test instance.

2
00:00:03.138 --> 00:00:04.875
It's not run by the authors.

3
00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:09.597
You need a test instance, never
production: Sequel Server 2022 or later,

4
00:00:09.597 --> 00:00:14.401
not a failover cluster instance,
Arc-enabled in a commercial Azure test

5
00:00:14.401 --> 00:00:17.413
subscription, which is
where a Microsoft 365

6
00:00:17.413 --> 00:00:20.100
G C C Moderate tenant's
Arc resources live.

7
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.069
It needs Entra authentication
configured, an Entra admin set,

8
00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:27.337
as in Module 3, and a
certificate your client trusts.

9
00:00:27.337 --> 00:00:29.995
Write a one-row mapping
for one Windows login,

10
00:00:29.995 --> 00:00:33.012
read the create script, and
run it as the Entra admin.

11
00:00:33.012 --> 00:00:35.388
That's the only step
that changes anything.

12
00:00:35.388 --> 00:00:38.125
Then sign in as a member
of the test Entra group,

13
00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:41.151
validate a real Entra
connection, and judge the run.

14
00:00:41.151 --> 00:00:45.217
To back it out, sign in as the
Entra admin, drop the database users

15
00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:49.050
the script created, then the
login, and delete the lab's files.

16
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.620
Drop login fails while
the login is connected,

17
00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.150
so wait for the member's session
to close and run that line again.
